  ImageLeft: {fileID: 0}
  Title: 
  Description: Bacteria are microscopic, single-celled organisms that thrive in diverse
    environments. These organisms can live in soil, the ocean and inside the human
    gut. Bacteria are classified as prokaryotes, which are single-celled organisms
    with a simple internal structure that lacks a nucleus, and contains DNA that either
    floats freely in a twisted, thread-like mass called the nucleoid, or in separate,
    circular pieces called plasmids. Ribosomes are the spherical units in the bacterial
    cell where proteins are assembled from individual amino acids using the information
    encoded in ribosomal RNA.
  ImageRight: {fileID: 0}
